  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling Access and Learning in Education (SCALE) - Remediation Pilot in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Key objectives include:&#x25cf; Developing and testing contextualised teaching and learning materials (TLMs) tailored to Malawi&#x2019;s educational context.&#x25cf; Developing a monitoring, measurement, and review system that ensures focus on children&#x2019;s foundational learning outcomes.&#x25cf; Building capacity within the MoE for governance, monitoring, and scaling of TaRL.&#x25cf; Enhancing teacher, mentor, and school leader training to deliver quality remedial education.&#x25cf; Addressing gender equity and inclusivity for learners with diverse needs.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed remediation pilot in Malawi seeks to improve foundational literacy and numeracy outcomes for primary school learners by integrating evidence-based remedial teaching practices. This initiative aligns with Malawi&#x2019;s National Reading and Numeracy Programs (NRP/NNP) and focuses on institutional sustainability and scalability. The proposed remediation pilot also fits with FCDO priorities by addressing foundational learning challenges, supporting sustainable and scalable national systems, and promoting inclusive and equitable education outcomes. Finally, the project supports the realisation of several SDGs: SDG 4 (Quality Education) by improving literacy, numeracy, and education system capacity; SDG 5 (Gender Equality) by addressing barriers for girls and promoting inclusivity; SDG 10 (Reduced Inequalities) by supporting marginalized learners; and SDG 17 (Partnerships for the Goals) through collaboration with Malawi&#x2019;s Ministry of Education and local partners.</narrative>
  </description>
